cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NoOrg in your work, please cite this repository."
title: "NoOrg: A Typed, Durable Runtime for Explicit Agent Execution"
abstract: >-
  NoOrg is a typed TypeScript runtime for coordinating explicitly registered
  agents through a durable task state machine, with explicit language-model
  providers, bounded lifecycle behavior, and an evidence-gated release
  process documented in a reproducible manuscript.
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6232-9096"
  - name: "Active Inference Institute"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - task orchestration
  - TypeScript
  - active inference
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
version: 2.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ActiveInferenceInstitute/NoOrg"
